{{define "title"}}Pricing - MPP Viewer{{end}}

{{define "main"}}
<main class="page page--text centered">
  <div class="page__head">
    <h1>Pricing</h1>
  </div>

  {{with .Flash}}<p class="flash">{{.}}</p>{{end}}

  <p class="lead">
    Opening a plan is free and always will be. What is paid for is the second party - the
    colleague who opens your schedule through a link without installing anything.
  </p>

  <div class="plans__wrap">
    <table class="plans">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th></th>
          <th>No account</th>
          <th>Free account</th>
          <th class="plans__best">Pro</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Open and read a plan</td>
          <td class="plans__yes"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
          <td class="plans__yes"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
          <td class="plans__yes plans__best"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Export to Excel</td>
          <td class="plans__yes"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
          <td class="plans__yes"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
          <td class="plans__yes plans__best"><span class="sr-only">Yes</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Keep plans to come back to</td>
          <td class="plans__none"><span class="sr-only">-</span></td>
          <td>20 plans</td>
          <td class="plans__best">Unlimited</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Share a read-only link</td>
          <td class="plans__none"><span class="sr-only">-</span></td>
          <td>2 at a time</td>
          <td class="plans__best">Unlimited</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Upload size</td>
          <td>10 MB</td>
          <td>10 MB</td>
          <td class="plans__best">50 MB</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="plans__note">
    Sharing needs a confirmed email address on any plan. A link sent from an unproven mailbox is
    a reputation problem, so the address is checked once before the first link goes out.
  </p>

  <h2>Pro is free right now</h2>

  <p>
    The first accounts to ask get Pro at no cost, and <strong>keep it</strong> - it does not
    expire and turns into nothing later. That is a deliberate trade: at this stage the product
    needs people using it and telling us what breaks far more than it needs the money.
  </p>

  <p>
    There is no price yet, and inventing one to fill this page would be dishonest. When Pro
    starts costing something, the amount and the billing terms will appear here and in the terms
    of use, and early accounts keep what they were given.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>Do I have to pay to read a file someone sent me?</dt>
    <dd>No, and you do not need an account either. Drop the file, read the chart, download the spreadsheet if you want one. Nothing is stored and nothing is charged.</dd>

    <dt>What happens when early access ends?</dt>
    <dd>Accounts that already have Pro keep it. New accounts will see a price here. Nothing you saved is taken away and no plan stops opening.</dd>

    <dt>What happens to my plans if I stay on the free tier?</dt>
    <dd>They stay. The free tier keeps up to 20 saved plans and 2 live share links; going over the cap stops new saves, it never deletes an old one.</dd>

    <dt>Is there anything to cancel?</dt>
    <dd>Not today - there is no payment and no billing cycle to end. You can delete your account from the account page at any time, which removes every plan and link with it.</dd>
  </dl>
</main>

{{template "sitefooter" .}}
{{end}}
